{
  "_id": "hTOsC2mYsjb6fLBw",
  "name": "Songal's Elemental Suffusion",
  "type": "spell",
  "img": "icons/magic/air/wind-vortex-swirl-blue-purple.webp",
  "folder": "yL1ACoe0mGMzSWKO",
  "sort": 0,
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You fill yourself with the elemental power of genies and gain the following benefits until the spell ends.</p><p><strong>Elemental Immunity.</strong> When you cast the spell, choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder damage. You have Resistance to the chosen type.</p><p><strong>Elemental Pulse.</strong> When you cast the spell, and at the start of each of your later turns, you release a burst of elemental energy in a 15-foot Emanation originating from you. Each creature of your choice in it makes a Dexterity saving throw. On a failure, it takes 2d6 Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder damage (your choice) and has the &amp;Reference[prone apply=false]{Prone} condition; on a success, it takes half as much damage only.</p><p><strong>Flight.</strong> You gain a Fly Speed of 30 feet and can hover.</p><p><strong>Casting as a Circle Spell.</strong> Cast as a Circle spell, its casting time becomes 1 minute and its duration Concentration, up to 10 minutes. For each secondary caster who takes part, you can choose one additional creature, up to nine more, which also gains the spell’s benefits for the duration. When the spell is cast, each secondary caster must expend a level 2+ spell slot; otherwise, the spell fails.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
